 #!/usr/bin/env python3
 """
-ZMQ TCP ONNX Runtime Client
+ZMQ detector service for Frigate's `zmq` detector plugin.
 
-This client connects to the ZMQ TCP proxy, accepts tensor inputs,
-runs inference via a pluggable backend (ONNX Runtime CPU / CoreML today,
-see backends.py) and returns detection results.
-
-Protocol:
-- Receives multipart messages: [header_json_bytes, tensor_bytes]
-- Header contains shape and dtype information
-- Runs ONNX inference on the tensor
-- Returns results in the expected format: [20, 6] float32 array
+Accepts tensor inputs over ZMQ, runs inference via a pluggable backend
+(backends.py: ONNX Runtime CPU / CoreML / ncnn / MNN-Vulkan) and returns
+detection results.
+
+Protocol (unchanged, exactly what frigate/detectors/plugins/zmq_ipc.py speaks):
+- Request: multipart [header_json_bytes, tensor_bytes]; the header carries
