+## MNN batch-mode library (`mnn-batch/`, 2026-09-06)
+
+Phase 1 of the GPU runtime work (`~/gpu-opt/PHASE1_RUNTIME.md`) found that
+MNN's Vulkan backend records one `VkCommandBuffer` per op, which Honeykrisp turns into
+~474 GPU control streams per inference (half the GPU time idle, 6 ms of CPU in
+`queue_submit`). MNN's existing `MNN_GPU_RECORD_BATCH` mode records the whole graph
+into one command buffer; the patch
+`~/gpu-opt/patches/mnn/0001-Vulkan-record-the-whole-graph-into-one-command-buffe.patch`
+makes it the Vulkan default, so the shim needs no change (`cfg.numThread = 1` -> gpu
+mode 0x1 -> `TUNING_NONE | RECORD_BATCH` on the patched lib; opt-out is
+`MNN_GPU_RECORD_OP`).
+
+* `mnn-batch/src/` = `git archive 330e565` of `~/gpu-opt/MNN` (branch
+  `gpu-opt`): upstream `bef71b9` (exactly what `../research/MNN-src` is) + `11fdc84`
+  (the same `-D__STRICT_ANSI__` removal the research tree carries uncommitted) +
+  `330e565` (the patch). `mnn-batch/PROVENANCE.txt` records this.
+* `mnn-batch/build.sh` configures and builds it (`-DMNN_VULKAN=ON -DMNN_VULKAN_IMAGE=ON
+  -DMNN_OPENCL=OFF -DMNN_ARM82=ON`, tools/benchmark off, `ninja -j4`, ~2 min; run it
+  as `systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=5G mnn-batch/build.sh`) and copies the
+  result to `mnn-batch/lib/libMNN.so`. The 2026-09-06 build is md5-identical
+  (`d38a258b…`) to the library Phase 1 measured (`~/gpu-opt/MNN/build/libMNN.so`).
+  The research library `../research/MNN-src/build/libMNN.so` is untouched and remains
+  the shim's rpath default.
+* The service selects it with two `Environment=` lines in the unit:
+  `DETECTOR_VULKAN_PREFERENCE=mnn-vulkan,ncnn-vulkan` and
+  `DETECTOR_MNN_LIB=~/frigate/detector/mnn-batch/lib/libMNN.so` (`--backend
+  vulkan` stays; if mnn-vulkan cannot initialise the alias falls through to ncnn-vulkan,
+  then to cpu). The copy `./frigate-detector.service` already contains them.
+
